# Empty since the Postgres cutover (2026-09-12), and kept only so the path
# still resolves for anything that assumes it.
#
# This used to hold SQLite snapshots written by trade.sh::backup_database(),
# which was itself never called -- the six files were manual pre-repair copies
# from the Sep 2026 data fixes, all superseded (each held MORE historical_moves
# rows than production, because they predate the duplicate cleanup).
#
# ⚠️ This note previously said those six were "removed here." That was only
# true on the Mac. the server still had all six -- 49MB of them -- until 2026-09-12,
# because the cutover cleaned one host and the note was written as if it had
# cleaned both. Same shape as the Sep 8 propagation failure that motivated
# consolidating onto one database in the first place: "done" and "done
# everywhere" are separate claims. Both hosts are now genuinely empty here.
#
# Backups now live on the server: a host-side pg-backup script, run nightly by
# trading-pg-backup.timer, writing pg_dump -Fc to local disk, a backup host and Google
# Drive -- verified monthly by RESTORING the dump, not
# by assuming it. To recover data, use 2.0/scripts/restore_database.sh, which
# restores side by side and leaves production alone unless told otherwise.
